WEBVTT

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.970
Seeking out a single ray of light,
hito-suji no hikari wo motome

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:34.210
All I can do is wander on, no matter how far.
hitasura doko made mo tada samayou

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:42.950
As I breathe a sigh not unlike surrender,
akirame ni nita tameiki wo tsuki-nagara

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:52.270
I don't want to fear how I've been hurt, all the time.
kizutsuku koto wo osoretaku nai yo itsu mo

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.650
Set me free now!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.060
Come on, let it all go, to the far reaches of time,
saa tokihanate subete toki no kanata ni

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.080
From that which binds the soul!
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.910
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo
From that which binds the soul!

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.200
For my heartbeat!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.690
Make freedom your weapon,
jiyuu wo buki ni

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:11.760
And you are sure to attain it!
kitto te ni ireru no yo

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.470
kitto te ni ireru no yo
And you are sure to attain it!

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:15.510
The power to believe and dream is there
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:21.590
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo
The power to believe and dream is there

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:21.630
for you to go on living.
ikite yuku tame ni

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.960
ikite yuku tame ni
for you to go on living.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.010
Who is it that told you this route would be a piece of cake!?

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.670
It is a piece of cake!

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.840
That is, it would have been,

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.350
if a certain somebody hadn't decided we should charge our way into this sandstorm.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.890
I guess so...

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.360
Stay sharp!

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.360
Right, right.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:17.660
One's coming! A big one!

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:40.720
Yuji!!

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.330
Out of my way, you insect bastard!

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.300
Yuji!

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.220
Where am I...?

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:27.660
Marlene...

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.500
Where's Marlene?

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.680
No, you shouldn't move yet!

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:46.880
Good. If you hadn't opened your eyes soon, I don't know what I would have done.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.340
Where is this?

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.900
We move around, looking for food for our goats.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.680
Along the way, we found you slumped over.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:21.120
So that's it. Thanks for saving me.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.660
Are you okay!?

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:31.300
Sorry.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.960
So he's finally come to?

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.630
Dad!

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:39.640
You can let us take care of you until your injuries heal.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:42.300
It's milking time.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.310
What's your name?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.320
Yuji, Kaido Yuji.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:55.980
Yuji, huh? What an unusual name. Yuji. Yuji... How strange!

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.320
Um... so what's your name?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.060
Me? Elena.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:08.330
Elena, huh?

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.270
Marlene... Dice... Are you okay?

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.680
You don't need to be worrying about Yuji.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.350
He may be young, but he's a full-fledged man.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:28.020
I'm sure he can at least look after himself.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.060
Right?

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:35.290
Don't look so scared. Are you really that worried about Yuji?

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:40.960
Of course. I am headed to Baikonur with the Sample. I have been given...

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.300
- this important duty, huh?

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.640
How commendable.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:51.980
Is your duty all that important? There's something else important to you, ain't there?

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:57.990
Nonsense! There is nothing more important than duty. Not to me right now...

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:00.220
There, that does it.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.660
We're off!

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:22.680
We're leaving already?

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:27.480
Mm-hm, we have to look for other lands to feed our goats.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:40.790
But, if you don't know where or when you'll be attacked by the Blue,

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.630
why not run away to some safe place?

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:47.970
Safe place? And where would that be?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.900
Well, that is...

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:15.560
Since everywhere we go is the same, we never change.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:19.120
We are just born into this land, grow up, and die.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.680
Somehow, I envy you.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:33.270
Being able to live like this.

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:37.620
Really? In that case, you could just live among us too, Yuji!

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.990
These are new bullet holes... test firing?

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:16.990
Yeah, this was quite the poorly-behaved group.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:21.660
Who are they? If soldiers were to pull something like this, they'd be disciplined.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:24.170
If they were normal soldiers, that is.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.610
Say, have you seen Yuji?

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.280
Not sure. I saw someone headed for the lake a while ago.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.290
Really? Thanks!

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:51.620
Elena, stop constantly looking after strangers and start taking care of me!

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:52.960
I'll think about it!

00:08:56.370 --> 00:09:02.030
Don't get in too deep over him. He is from a different world, after all.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:20.320
It's supposed to be in this direction-Baikonur. No reason I should see it, I guess.

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:21.980
We think alike!

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:24.990
Elena?

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:30.660
This is my favorite spot. It's pretty, how you can see the whole lake, isn't it?

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:34.600
Huh? Y- yeah, sure is.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.600
Say, Yuji, have you ever seen the ocean?

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.610
The ocean?

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.940
When I was a child, I heard something from my late grandpa.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:47.280
He said the ocean was many times as vast as this. Hard for me to believe, though.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.150
Many times doesn't even cover it!

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:51.950
Compared to the ocean, this is like a puddle.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:52.950
Really!?

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:57.960
Yeah. Blue and wide, stretching out forever.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:02.290
Well, if the lake is like this, then this much?

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:07.300
Uh uh, not quite.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.630
Then, this much!

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.300
Not even close.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:13.970
Then, how much!?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:17.640
Let's see...

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:19.650
Yuji?

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.010
The same as the sky. As far as you can see!

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:39.760
Wow. The ocean is incredible, huh? Sometime... will you show it to me?

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:04.660
What is it!?

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:23.340
So now, what sort of catch will we have this time?

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:51.770
We are the Kyzyl Kum area guard, 4th independent squad.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:56.340
We are currently conducting a campaign to exterminate the Blue.

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:59.810
We are unable to contact our base, and our supplies are running out.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:03.340
As such, we would like to ask for your cooperation.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:07.010
We have need of your food and materials and such.

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:08.150
We refuse!

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:15.230
Go back to where you came from!

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:20.030
We have absolutely nothing to share with you miscreants!

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:21.540
Shut up!

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:34.310
Dad!

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:39.320
If it weren't for us, you'd all have been killed by the Blue already!

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:40.980
Enough!

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:45.720
If that is how you feel, then we will just have to make you cooperate our own way!

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:59.340
This is great! We're getting some target practice!

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:04.000
Ain't you got anything besides this!? Military rations were far better than this!

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:12.680
How awful! How terribly awful!

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:13.450
Elena!

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:22.360
Stop it!

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:24.370
Get off of our land!

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.030
Elena! Stay back!

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:38.640
Elena!

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:45.310
This will be my trophy! You guys enjoy yourselves however you want!

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:48.320
Elena!

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:49.650
Yuji!

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:51.450
Hm!? What do you want!?

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:57.460
W- what do you think you're doing, you...!?

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:01.000
H- hey, kid!

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.440
Stop that!

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:19.680
Leave the rest to me, Elena!

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:20.550
Yuji!

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:32.300
Why!? Why is there someone in a place like this that can operate an Armor Shrike!?

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:39.270
What!?

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:53.750
Withdraw! Withdraw!

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:13.770
Everyone, you can relax now! They've learned their lesson, and... huh?

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:51.300
I'll help you, too.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:14.000
You should know well enough yourself.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:17.630
He's someone who is incompatible with us.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.670
Elena!

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:30.650
I wouldn't know such a thing!

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:53.840
Nomads, huh? I'm surprised there are still people like that around!

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:00.640
Yuji...

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.980
What?

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:46.630
Elena...

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:53.000
Thank goodness! I was worried that maybe you had gone off somewhere!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:56.970
You found a map, right?

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:01.980
Yeah, the survival kit in the Armor Shrike was outfitted with one.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.310
Are you leaving, Yuji?

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:08.180
I was thinking that if I went to Baikonur, something would change.

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:15.320
I thought I knew what lay ahead. But...

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:20.660
Now I'm not so sure. Was it really all that meaningful, or instead...

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:22.990
If so...

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:29.990
It doesn't have to change, I don't think. You don't have to force a change.

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:32.070
No matter where you go...

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:36.270
No matter where you live, Yuji, you'll still be Yuji, you know.

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:37.280
Elena...

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:40.410
And so, stay here.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:44.210
Don't go anywhere...

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:21.320
This cold is really hard on an old man!

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.690
Hey, time to change the guard.

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:56.290
Isn't that the nicest face?

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.670
Yuji?

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.200
Yuji...

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:39.690
Although the days when we smiled again and again
hohoemi kasaneta hibi ga

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:45.820
Have passed away into dreams,
maboroshi ni natte mo

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:54.970
I will surely not lose my way.
watashi wa kitto mayowanai

00:21:55.090 --> 00:22:01.140
To go on to the future,
mirai ni yuku tame ni

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:07.560
To become an adult,
otona ni naru tame ni

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:14.750
I again recall now the memories
mogaite kita omoide wo kokoro de

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:19.910
twisting in my heart.
ima wa kurikaesu

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:25.970
I'm living in one time,
hitotsu no toki wo iki

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:32.250
While choosing two dreams,
futatsu no yume erabi

00:22:32.860 --> 00:22:39.730
And love taught me what it means...
soshite ai ga oshiete kureta yo ne

00:22:39.910 --> 00:22:46.590
to cherish someone.
hito wo omou imi

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:54.700
I'm not going to Baikonur!

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:57.700
Are you serious, Yuji?

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.710
After all, Marlene, you're just doing this out of duty.

00:23:01.770 --> 00:23:06.040
In that case, I'll force you to do as I say!

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:10.950
If you intend to shoot Yuji, go ahead and shoot me as well!
